# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we will implement a workflow to sample from a Clifford circuit and use the ``qiskit-paulice`` package to boost the fidelity of the measured distribution by applying [spacetime Pauli checks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) throughout the circuit. Spacetime Pauli checks are similar to [coherent Pauli checks (CPC)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937) in that a Clifford \"payload\" circuit is entangled to some ancillary qubits in order to \"check\" certain invariants in the circuit. Measurement of the ancillas produces a syndrome that is used to determine whether a logical error was detected during execution of the circuit. Postselecting only samples where no error was detected can improve the fidelity of sampled distributions at the expense of decreasing postselection rates. The key difference between CPC and spacetime checks is that measuring CPC syndromes requires measuring time localized, high weight operators. On qubit topologies with limited connectivity, such as heavy hex, implementing these checks requires many SWAP gates, often making the circuit too deep to run in practice. Implementing Pauli checks as spacetime codes allows them to be distributed throughout the payload circuit, allowing for a hardware efficient qubit encoding that remains effective at detecting logical errors during circuit execution. The primary role of the ``qiskit-paulice`` package is to find and insert valid spacetime Pauli checks into locations in the circuit that both maximize error detection effectiveness and minimize qubit overhead.\n"
msgstr "Sa tutorial na ito, magpapatupad tayo ng workflow para mag-sample mula sa isang Clifford circuit at gagamitin ang package na ``qiskit-paulice`` para pataasin ang fidelity ng nasukat na distribusyon sa pamamagitan ng paglalapat ng [spacetime Pauli checks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) sa buong circuit. Katulad ng [coherent Pauli checks (CPC)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937) ang spacetime Pauli checks dahil ang isang Clifford na \"payload\" circuit ay ina-entangle sa ilang ancillary qubit para \"i-check\" ang ilang invariant sa circuit. Ang pagsukat sa mga ancilla ay gumagawa ng syndrome na ginagamit para matukoy kung may logical error na nakita habang isinasagawa ang circuit. Ang pag-postselect lang ng mga sample na walang nakitang error ay maaaring magpabuti ng fidelity ng mga na-sample na distribusyon kapalit ng pagbaba ng postselection rate. Ang pangunahing pagkakaiba ng CPC at spacetime checks ay ang pagsukat ng mga CPC syndrome ay nangangailangan ng pagsukat ng mga operator na time-localized at mataas ang weight. Sa mga qubit topology na limitado ang connectivity, tulad ng heavy hex, ang pagpapatupad ng mga check na ito ay nangangailangan ng maraming SWAP gate, na madalas ginagawang masyadong malalim ang circuit para patakbuhin sa praktika. Ang pagpapatupad ng mga Pauli check bilang spacetime code ay nagpapahintulot na ipamahagi ang mga ito sa buong payload circuit, na nagbibigay-daan sa hardware-efficient na qubit encoding na nananatiling epektibo sa pagtukoy ng mga logical error habang isinasagawa ang circuit. Ang pangunahing papel ng package na ``qiskit-paulice`` ay maghanap at magpasok ng mga wastong spacetime Pauli check sa mga lokasyon ng circuit na parehong nagpapalaki ng bisa ng error detection at nagpapaliit ng qubit overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial implements a workflow for boosting the fidelity of the distribution sampled from a quantum circuit using spacetime checks. Since we will use a Clifford circuit, we can estimate the fidelity straightforwardly from the averaged expectation values of the stabilizers of the circuit. We will follow these steps:\n"
msgstr "Nagpapatupad ang tutorial na ito ng workflow para pataasin ang fidelity ng distribusyong na-sample mula sa isang quantum circuit gamit ang spacetime checks. Dahil gagamit tayo ng Clifford circuit, madali nating matatantya ang fidelity mula sa averaged expectation value ng mga stabilizer ng circuit. Susundin natin ang mga hakbang na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Create a circuit**: Shallow 1D brickwork random Clifford circuit used to visualize the checks.\n"
msgstr "**Gumawa ng circuit**: Mababaw na 1D brickwork na random Clifford circuit na ginagamit para i-visualize ang mga check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Identify qubits as targets for checks**: Map the circuit to physical qubits on the ``ibm_boston`` Heron QPU and identify qubits with neighboring ancillas.\n"
msgstr "**Tukuyin ang mga qubit bilang target ng mga check**: I-map ang circuit sa mga pisikal na qubit sa ``ibm_boston`` Heron QPU at tukuyin ang mga qubit na may katabing ancilla.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Transpile the circuit to the backend**: Select a qubit layout and translate the circuit gates into the native gate set of ``ibm_boston``.\n"
msgstr "**I-transpile ang circuit sa backend**: Pumili ng qubit layout at isalin ang mga gate ng circuit sa native gate set ng ``ibm_boston``.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Create a noise model from backend data**: Generate a rough noise model based on backend benchmark data. This noise data will be used to score the effectiveness of each additional check.\n"
msgstr "**Gumawa ng noise model mula sa data ng backend**: Gumawa ng magaspang na noise model batay sa benchmark data ng backend. Gagamitin ang noise data na ito para i-score ang bisa ng bawat karagdagang check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Visualize Pauli checks**: Add some Pauli checks to the shallow circuit, so we can visualize how the checks are added.\n"
msgstr "**I-visualize ang mga Pauli check**: Magdagdag ng ilang Pauli check sa mababaw na circuit, para makita natin kung paano idinaragdag ang mga check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Determine stabilizers to measure**: Increase the depth of the circuit to increase the impact of gate noise. Randomly sample a subset of stabilizers of the deeper circuit.\n"
msgstr "**Tukuyin ang mga stabilizer na susukatin**: Dagdagan ang depth ng circuit para lumaki ang epekto ng gate noise. Mag-sample nang random ng subset ng mga stabilizer ng mas malalim na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Find good checks for the whole state**: Find one set of checks for the stabilizers of the state the circuit prepares. Such checks are valid whatever is measured afterwards, so the same checked circuit serves every sampled stabilizer.\n"
msgstr "**Maghanap ng magagandang check para sa buong state**: Maghanap ng isang set ng mga check para sa mga stabilizer ng state na inihahanda ng circuit. Wasto ang mga ganitong check anuman ang susukatin pagkatapos, kaya iisang checked circuit ang magagamit para sa bawat na-sample na stabilizer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '8. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sample from the noisy circuit**: Measure the bare and checked circuits in the basis of each sampled stabilizer with [samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic), and sample them with the ``Executor`` primitive on a noisy simulator that uses the same depolarizing noise that was used to find the checks.\n"
msgstr "**Mag-sample mula sa maingay na circuit**: Sukatin ang bare at checked na mga circuit sa basis ng bawat na-sample na stabilizer gamit ang [samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic), at i-sample ang mga ito gamit ang ``Executor`` primitive sa isang maingay na simulator na gumagamit ng parehong depolarizing noise na ginamit sa paghahanap ng mga check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '9. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Postselect checked circuit samples with no detected errors**: Remove samples which fail at least one check. Calculate expectation values for the bare noisy circuit and the circuit containing checks.\n"
msgstr "**I-postselect ang mga sample ng checked circuit na walang nakitang error**: Alisin ang mga sample na bumagsak sa kahit isang check. Kalkulahin ang mga expectation value para sa bare na maingay na circuit at sa circuit na may mga check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '10. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compare fidelities of original and postselected noisy states**: Show that postselecting only samples with no detected errors improves the estimated fidelity of the noisy state.\n"
msgstr "**Ihambing ang mga fidelity ng orihinal at postselected na maingay na state**: Ipakita na ang pag-postselect lang ng mga sample na walang nakitang error ay nagpapabuti sa tinatantyang fidelity ng maingay na state.\n"

