msgid "6. Determine stabilizers to measure {#6-determine-stabilizers-to-measure}"
msgstr "6. Tukuyin ang mga stabilizer na susukatin {#6-determine-stabilizers-to-measure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To test the performance of the error detection we will estimate the fidelity of the stabilizer state, $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, that the circuit ideally prepares against the noisy state, $\\rho$, the hardware actually outputs. The projector onto the pure stabilizer state, $|\\psi\\rangle$, is defined to be the uniform average over the $2^n$ elements of its stabilizer group $\\mathcal{S}$:\n"
msgstr "Para subukan ang performance ng error detection, tatantyahin natin ang fidelity ng stabilizer state, $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, na ideal na inihahanda ng circuit, laban sa maingay na state, $\\rho$, na aktwal na inilalabas ng hardware. Ang projector sa purong stabilizer state, $|\\psi\\rangle$, ay tinutukoy bilang uniform na average sa $2^n$ elemento ng stabilizer group nito na $\\mathcal{S}$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = \\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} G$$\n"
msgstr "$$|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = \\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} G$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plugging this into the fidelity equation, we see that the fidelity of noisy state, $\\rho$, is equivalent to the average expectation value of all stabilizers, $G \\in \\mathcal{S}$, with respect to $\\rho$:\n"
msgstr "Sa pagsasaksak nito sa fidelity equation, makikita natin na ang fidelity ng maingay na state, $\\rho$, ay katumbas ng average na expectation value ng lahat ng stabilizer, $G \\in \\mathcal{S}$, kaugnay ng $\\rho$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$F = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi|) = \\mathrm{Tr}({\\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\rho G}) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho G) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\langle G \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"
msgstr "$$F = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi|) = \\mathrm{Tr}({\\frac{1}{2^n}\\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\rho G}) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho G) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{G \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\langle G \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For larger problems, measuring (or even enumerating) all $2^n$ stabilizers is infeasible, so fidelity is often estimated by measuring a random sample of stabilizers. Sampling $M$ stabilizers $G_1, \\ldots, G_M$ uniformly at random from $\\mathcal{S}$ gives an unbiased estimator of the fidelity, $\\hat F_M$,\n"
msgstr "Para sa mas malalaking problema, imposible ang pagsukat (o kahit ang pag-enumerate) sa lahat ng $2^n$ stabilizer, kaya madalas na tinatantya ang fidelity sa pamamagitan ng pagsukat ng random na sample ng mga stabilizer. Ang pag-sample ng $M$ stabilizer na $G_1, \\ldots, G_M$ nang uniform at random mula sa $\\mathcal{S}$ ay nagbibigay ng unbiased estimator ng fidelity, $\\hat F_M$,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\\hat F_M = \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{i=1}^M \\langle G_i \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"
"For this experiment we will make the circuit much deeper to enhance the effect of gate noise, and we will add checks to every qubit with a neighboring ancilla qubit. While there are more sophisticated ways to sample stabilizers to estimate fidelity, in this example we will sample $100$ stabilizers with uniform probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\\hat F_M = \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{i=1}^M \\langle G_i \\rangle_\\rho$$\n"
"Para sa eksperimentong ito, gagawin nating mas malalim ang circuit para palakasin ang epekto ng gate noise, at magdaragdag tayo ng mga check sa bawat qubit na may katabing ancilla qubit. Bagama't may mas sopistikadong paraan para mag-sample ng mga stabilizer para tantyahin ang fidelity, sa halimbawang ito ay magsa-sample tayo ng $100$ stabilizer na may uniform na probability.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Find good checks for the whole state {#7-find-good-checks-for-the-whole-state}"
msgstr "7. Maghanap ng magagandang check para sa buong state {#7-find-good-checks-for-the-whole-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We find one set of checks for the deep circuit exactly as in step 5. Since the checks read only their ancillas, the same checked circuit serves every sampled stabilizer. The returned circuits measure only the check ancillas, so we will add the payload measurements in the next step.\n"
msgstr "Naghahanap tayo ng isang set ng mga check para sa malalim na circuit, eksaktong tulad ng sa hakbang 5. Dahil ang mga check ay ancilla lang nila ang binabasa, iisang checked circuit ang magagamit para sa bawat na-sample na stabilizer. Ang mga ibinalik na circuit ay ang mga check ancilla lang ang sinusukat, kaya idaragdag natin ang mga payload measurement sa susunod na hakbang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Sample from the noisy circuit {#8-sample-from-the-noisy-circuit}"
msgstr "8. Mag-sample mula sa maingay na circuit {#8-sample-from-the-noisy-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We sample every variant, from the bare payload to the circuit with all ``7`` checks, for each sampled stabilizer. The variant with zero checks is the bare payload with the same measurements, so it serves as the noisy reference. Instead of appending the basis rotation of every stabilizer to a copy of every variant, we let [samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) choose the measurement basis at sampling time. For each variant we:\n"
msgstr "Sina-sample natin ang bawat variant, mula sa bare payload hanggang sa circuit na may lahat ng ``7`` check, para sa bawat na-sample na stabilizer. Ang variant na walang check ay ang bare payload na may parehong mga measurement, kaya ito ang nagsisilbing maingay na reference. Sa halip na idugtong ang basis rotation ng bawat stabilizer sa kopya ng bawat variant, hinahayaan nating piliin ng [samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) ang measurement basis sa oras ng pag-sample. Para sa bawat variant:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the payload and group the terminal measurements into a box with samplomatic's boxing pass manager. The box carries a ``ChangeBasis`` annotation, so ``build`` returns a template circuit whose basis-changing gates are parameterized, along with a samplex that computes the parameters for a requested basis.\n"
msgstr "Sukatin ang payload at i-grupo ang mga terminal measurement sa isang box gamit ang boxing pass manager ng samplomatic. Ang box ay may dalang ``ChangeBasis`` annotation, kaya ang ``build`` ay nagbabalik ng template circuit na ang mga basis-changing gate ay parameterized, kasama ang samplex na nagkakalkula ng mga parameter para sa hiniling na basis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add the template and samplex to a ``QuantumProgram``. The samplex takes one measurement basis per qubit in the box, in ascending physical order, encoded as $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, $Y=3$. Passing an array of bases with a leading axis of length ``100`` makes a single item measure all ``100`` stabilizers: the payload in each stabilizer's basis and the ancillas in $Z$. A qubit outside a stabilizer's support is also measured in $Z$, and its bit is ignored when the stabilizer's expectation value is computed.\n"
msgstr "Idagdag ang template at samplex sa isang ``QuantumProgram``. Ang samplex ay kumukuha ng isang measurement basis bawat qubit sa box, sa pataas na pisikal na pagkakasunod, na naka-encode bilang $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, $Y=3$. Ang pagpasa ng array ng mga basis na may leading axis na may haba na ``100`` ay nagpapasukat sa iisang item ng lahat ng ``100`` stabilizer: ang payload sa basis ng bawat stabilizer at ang mga ancilla sa $Z$. Ang qubit na nasa labas ng support ng isang stabilizer ay sinusukat din sa $Z$, at binabalewala ang bit nito kapag kinakalkula ang expectation value ng stabilizer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ``Executor`` primitive from ``qiskit-ibm-runtime`` runs the whole program in one job. Given an ``AerSimulator`` in place of a QPU it runs locally on that simulator, so we hand it one with the same depolarizing gate noise we used to find the checks, and use the stabilizer method since all of the circuits are Clifford. Qiskit Aer is needed only to build this simulator: the local mode takes the seed from the ``Executor`` options but ignores their ``noise_model``, so the noise must be set on the simulator itself. Passing a QPU backend instead would run the same program on hardware. Once the simulations are complete, we will calculate the postselection rate and expectation values to get a feel for how well the error detection worked before visualizing the data.\n"
msgstr "Pinapatakbo ng ``Executor`` primitive mula sa ``qiskit-ibm-runtime`` ang buong program sa isang job. Kapag binigyan ng ``AerSimulator`` bilang kapalit ng QPU, tumatakbo ito nang lokal sa simulator na iyon, kaya binibigyan natin ito ng may parehong depolarizing gate noise na ginamit natin sa paghahanap ng mga check, at ginagamit ang stabilizer method dahil Clifford ang lahat ng circuit. Kailangan lang ang Qiskit Aer para buuin ang simulator na ito: kinukuha ng local mode ang seed mula sa mga opsyon ng ``Executor`` pero binabalewala ang kanilang ``noise_model``, kaya dapat itakda ang noise sa mismong simulator. Ang pagpasa ng QPU backend sa halip ay magpapatakbo ng parehong program sa hardware. Kapag tapos na ang mga simulation, kakalkulahin natin ang postselection rate at mga expectation value para makakuha ng pakiramdam kung gaano kahusay gumana ang error detection bago i-visualize ang data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Postselect checked circuit samples {#9-postselect-checked-circuit-samples}"
msgstr "9. I-postselect ang mga sample ng checked circuit {#9-postselect-checked-circuit-samples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this package a check is implemented using entangling gates between one ancilla qubit and one target qubit. Each ancilla starts in $|0\\rangle$, so $Z_\\text{anc}$ stabilizes its input state. Forward propagating $Z_\\text{anc}$ from the beginning of the ancilla through the entire checked circuit yields $Z_\\text{anc}$ times a stabilizer of the prepared state, so the check passes if the ancilla bit is $0$. A sample is kept if every check passes.\n"
msgstr "Sa package na ito, ang isang check ay ipinapatupad gamit ang mga entangling gate sa pagitan ng isang ancilla qubit at isang target qubit. Bawat ancilla ay nagsisimula sa $|0\\rangle$, kaya ang $Z_\\text{anc}$ ay nag-istabilize sa input state nito. Ang forward propagation ng $Z_\\text{anc}$ mula sa simula ng ancilla sa buong checked circuit ay nagbibigay ng $Z_\\text{anc}$ na pinarami ng isang stabilizer ng inihandang state, kaya pumapasa ang check kung ang ancilla bit ay $0$. Itinatabi ang isang sample kung pumasa ang bawat check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The checked circuits measure the ancillas into the ``checks_c`` register, so a sample is kept if every bit of that register is ``0``. In general, the ``get_postselection_method`` method of the ``CheckedCircuit`` instances output from ``add_pauli_checks`` maps a shot's bitstring to the syndrome of every check at once; for checks found for the stabilizers of the prepared state, each syndrome is just its ancilla bit, so we read the register directly.\n"
msgstr "Sinusukat ng mga checked circuit ang mga ancilla papunta sa ``checks_c`` register, kaya itinatabi ang isang sample kung ``0`` ang bawat bit ng register na iyon. Sa pangkalahatan, ang method na ``get_postselection_method`` ng mga instance ng ``CheckedCircuit`` na output mula sa ``add_pauli_checks`` ay nagma-map ng bitstring ng isang shot sa syndrome ng bawat check nang sabay-sabay; para sa mga check na hinanap para sa mga stabilizer ng inihandang state, ang bawat syndrome ay ang ancilla bit lang nito, kaya binabasa natin nang direkta ang register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the chart, we see that adding more checks causes the postselection rate to go down. While the goal of error detection is to catch as many errors as possible, as postselection rate goes down more shots may be required to achieve some target accuracy. If the postselection rate drops too low, the number of shots needed to collect one logical sample may become prohibitive. In this example, the postselection rate seems to converge, implying that additional checks are contributing less additional detection capability. Although adding more Pauli checks generally provides greater error detection capability, it comes at a cost of increased circuit depth and an increase in sampling cost.\n"
msgstr "Sa chart, makikita natin na ang pagdaragdag ng mas maraming check ay nagpapababa sa postselection rate. Bagama't ang layunin ng error detection ay mahuli ang pinakamaraming error hangga't maaari, habang bumababa ang postselection rate, maaaring mas maraming shot ang kailanganin para maabot ang isang target na accuracy. Kung masyadong bumaba ang postselection rate, maaaring maging hadlang ang bilang ng mga shot na kailangan para makakolekta ng isang logical sample. Sa halimbawang ito, tila nagko-converge ang postselection rate, na nagpapahiwatig na ang karagdagang mga check ay mas kaunti na ang naidaragdag na kakayahan sa pagtukoy. Bagama't karaniwang nagbibigay ng mas malaking kakayahan sa error detection ang pagdaragdag ng mas maraming Pauli check, may kapalit itong dagdag na depth ng circuit at dagdag na gastos sa pag-sample.\n"

