# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "10. Compare fidelities of original and postselected noisy states {#10-compare-fidelities-of-original-and-postselected-noisy-states}"
msgstr "10. Ihambing ang mga fidelity ng orihinal at postselected na maingay na state {#10-compare-fidelities-of-original-and-postselected-noisy-states}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We see that postselecting only samples with no detected errors greatly improves the expectation value for every stabilizer, and thus improves the estimated fidelity of the stabilizer state. Although the postselected values were calculated using only the samples that passed every check, the expectation values are much more accurate and the sampled variance is lower. We can also now see that the postselection rate above was actually converging to a value similar to the noisy circuit fidelity. The postselection rate was converging because the checks were catching the vast majority of errors actually occurring during circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "Nakikita natin na ang pag-postselect lang ng mga sample na walang nakitang error ay lubos na nagpapabuti sa expectation value ng bawat stabilizer, at kaya nagpapabuti sa tinatantyang fidelity ng stabilizer state. Bagama't kinalkula ang mga postselected na value gamit lang ang mga sample na pumasa sa bawat check, mas tumpak ang mga expectation value at mas mababa ang sampled variance. Makikita rin natin ngayon na ang postselection rate sa itaas ay nagko-converge pala sa value na katulad ng fidelity ng maingay na circuit. Nagko-converge ang postselection rate dahil nahuhuli ng mga check ang karamihan sa mga error na aktwal na nangyayari habang isinasagawa ang circuit.\n"

